WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:07.872
Riley watched as the younger girls in the junior division pushed off, one by one.

2
00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:14.707
The riders started racing at thirty-second intervals, which meant that several riders shared the track at one time.

3
00:00:14.708 --> 00:00:21.206
As each rider rolled over the finish line, Coach Adams recorded his or her time.

4
00:00:21.207 --> 00:00:25.988
Finally only Quinn and Riley were left in the girls' junior division.

5
00:00:25.989 --> 00:00:33.695
The two girls mounted their bikes and waited for the whistle to signal Quinn's start.

6
00:00:33.696 --> 00:00:35.969
"Good luck," Quinn muttered.

7
00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:40.170
"Thanks," Riley said with a nod. "You too."

8
00:00:40.171 --> 00:00:54.263
The whistle blew, and Quinn dashed down the trail. Riley closed her eyes and breathed slowly, waiting for the next whistle.

9
00:00:54.264 --> 00:01:01.679
"I can do this," she told herself. "Wherever the brain goes, the body follows."

10
00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.915
She opened her eyes and was surprised to feel calm and in control.

11
00:01:06.916 --> 00:01:16.749
She adjusted her helmet and clipped her shoes into the pedals. Then the whistle sounded again.

12
00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:24.328
"My turn!" Riley thought. With one strong push, she burst down the track.

13
00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:32.131
Riley pumped the bike pedals hard, increasing her speed. She was glad to see that the dirt track was soft but not muddy.

14
00:01:32.132 --> 00:01:36.144
She took the first turn easily, leaning into the curve.

15
00:01:36.145 --> 00:01:41.474
After the second curve, the last few jitters seemed to leave her body.

16
00:01:41.475 --> 00:01:48.132
The first jump appeared. Riley pumped harder and stood up in the saddle.

17
00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:56.258
She bent over the handlebars and easily sailed over the jump, her mind focused on maintaining her weight and balance in the air.

18
00:01:56.259 --> 00:02:02.099
Both tires hit the ground together, and she sped off.

19
00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:09.201
"Smooth jump!" she thought with relief. Now she was actually having fun on the track!

20
00:02:09.202 --> 00:02:18.681
She shifted gears again and sped up. Soon the bike's speedometer read 12 miles per hour.

21
00:02:18.682 --> 00:02:24.195
"Perfect!" she thought. The second jump was coming, and she knew she could take it.

22
00:02:24.196 --> 00:02:38.924
The steps felt almost effortless as she performed them: speed up, stop pedaling, lift the bike, balance and stay airborne, and land.

23
00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:43.929
"Phew! I made it!" Riley thought happily.

24
00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:52.399
Suddenly she heard the crowd gasp. "Was that for Quinn?" Riley wondered. "Did something happen?"

25
00:02:52.400 --> 00:03:02.481
There was no sign of Quinn, so there was no way to know. Riley pumped harder, accelerating back up to 12 miles per hour.

26
00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:07.408
Riley was so focused on regaining speed that she forgot where she was on the track.

27
00:03:07.409 --> 00:03:13.137
After she took the next curve, she realized that another jump was at the end of the straightaway.

28
00:03:13.138 --> 00:03:19.395
It looked like a tricky one, with a mud pit below and a landing ramp a little off center.

29
00:03:19.396 --> 00:03:27.046
Riley gulped. "Uh-oh," she thought. "This is the jump where Jordan crashed."

30
00:03:27.047 --> 00:03:37.206
Just then Riley spotted motion on the trail ahead of her. It was Quinn, racing madly toward the jump.

31
00:03:37.207 --> 00:03:42.626
"That's strange," Riley thought. "Quinn should be farther ahead of me."

32
00:03:42.627 --> 00:03:48.776
She remembered the gasps from the crowd. Maybe something had happened to Quinn on the track.

33
00:03:48.777 --> 00:03:56.363
Riley knew she should be focused on her own ride. But she kept her eyes glued to Quinn as the other girl barreled toward the jump.

34
00:03:56.364 --> 00:04:01.200
Quinn's head was down, and she didn't appear to notice the jump coming at her.

35
00:04:01.201 --> 00:04:04.436
"Look up, look up!" Riley thought.

36
00:04:04.437 --> 00:04:15.343
At the last minute Riley saw her look up. But by now Quinn was going too fast to adjust her speed or her balance.

37
00:04:15.344 --> 00:04:21.420
Riley came to a full stop, watching anxiously as Quinn flew over the jump.

38
00:04:21.421 --> 00:04:25.664
Quinn's front tire dipped dangerously lower than the back tire.

39
00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:32.496
Quinn frantically tried to regain her balance, pulling up on the handlebars to straighten the wheels before landing.

40
00:04:32.497 --> 00:04:37.978
"She's not going to make it," Riley thought. "She's going to crash."

41
00:04:37.979 --> 00:04:43.737
Thud! Quinn's bike came down and hit the edge of the landing ramp with a sickening sound.

42
00:04:43.738 --> 00:04:49.808
The bike flipped, sending Quinn flying over the handlebars.

43
00:04:49.809 --> 00:04:58.397
The crowd gasped. Riley cringed, bracing herself to see Quinn break her fall improperly, with her hands.

44
00:04:58.398 --> 00:05:02.048
"Here it comes," she murmured.

45
00:05:02.049 --> 00:05:08.384
Instead Quinn tucked her arms into her sides and rolled onto the ground.

46
00:05:08.385 --> 00:05:13.968
The bike bounced away from her, splashing into the mud pit.

47
00:05:13.969 --> 00:05:22.977
The crowd cheered as Quinn quickly jumped up, covered in mud, and grabbed her bike.

48
00:05:22.978 --> 00:05:31.448
Just then Quinn looked up and spotted Riley watching her. Quinn flashed Riley a determined look as she jumped on her bike.

49
00:05:31.449 --> 00:05:38.359
With one mad push, Quinn got back on the trail and took off.

50
00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:47.019
Riley was so relieved that Quinn wasn't injured, it took her a second to realize that she herself had come to a stop.

51
00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:58.182
"Ack!" Riley cried as she began pedaling again. "You're not going to beat me, Quinn Evans!" She raced toward the jump.

52
00:05:58.183 --> 00:06:04.666
As Riley approached the jump, she saw that Quinn's spill had churned up the soft dirt on the jump ramp.

53
00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:09.759
Quinn's fall had also taken a big chunk of dirt out of the edge of the landing ramp.

54
00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:16.177
Even before she reached the jump, Riley knew her tires wouldn't have enough traction to hold the landing.

55
00:06:16.178 --> 00:06:19.904
Panic washed over her like cold water.

56
00:06:19.905 --> 00:06:30.232
"No!" Riley yelled, gritting her teeth and gripping the handlebars. She couldn't lose this race—or her spot on the team.

57
00:06:30.233 --> 00:06:40.392
She pedaled hard and hit the jump. Her back tire skidded in the soft dirt, but the bike lifted into the air.

58
00:06:40.393 --> 00:06:48.957
Riley rose up, up, over the mud pit, struggling to keep her balance. Then she braced for the impact of the landing.

59
00:06:48.958 --> 00:06:55.465
The front wheel landed perfectly, but the back wheel barely cleared the edge of the ramp.

60
00:06:55.466 --> 00:07:02.536
As her body flew off the bike, Riley closed her eyes. She tucked her arms in and bent her head.

61
00:07:02.537 --> 00:07:08.543
She hit the ground hard, sliding through the dirt and right off the trail.

62
00:07:08.544 --> 00:07:19.291
"Ouch!" Riley cried as pain shot through her shoulder. She rolled to a stop, breathing heavily.

63
00:07:19.292 --> 00:07:24.853
She waited for more pain, but to her surprise, only her shoulder ached.

64
00:07:24.854 --> 00:07:35.023
"I'm okay!" she told herself. "I'm still in this race!" She jumped up, her eyes scanning the mud pit for her bike.

65
00:07:35.024 --> 00:07:43.929
Riley yanked her bike out of the mud pit and jumped back on, flying down the track.

66
00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:48.991
"Focus," she reminded herself. "Eyes on the track."

67
00:07:48.992 --> 00:08:00.805
She had lost a lot of time, but maybe, with determination and focus, she could still win the race.

